01:31:46.160 --> 01:31:47.880
They're alerted and dangerous.

01:31:50.880 --> 01:31:54.480
Suggest continuing on to another galaxy.

01:31:57.090 --> 01:31:58.770
Total personnel.

01:32:00.670 --> 01:32:07.750
Blast. Destroy. Scout. Ship.

01:32:30.160 --> 01:32:37.900
Your people are one. That makes you happy, doesn't it?

01:32:47.480 --> 01:32:51.610
Never knew happiness or love or any emotion

01:32:51.610 --> 01:32:59.870
that came here to your birth and just began to learn.

01:33:31.660 --> 01:33:32.100
Marge.

01:33:50.830 --> 01:33:51.610
Get out of here, please.

01:34:43.980 --> 01:34:46.480
It was some disgusting ending there, wasn't it, boys?

01:34:47.110 --> 01:34:49.550
Oh, no, I don't mean Marge and Bill getting back together.

01:34:49.730 --> 01:34:54.250
No, I'm talking about like how the chief's hand just kind of melted there, you know?

01:34:54.370 --> 01:34:59.820
And then Bill just kind of looked kind of like digested oatmeal, you know what I mean?

01:35:00.000 --> 01:35:14.020
Oatmeal stains are no problem. As a matter of fact, I cover oatmeal stains in my other book, Sally McBride's House Cleaning Guide. Look it up under Chapter 4, which is titled, Have a Good Time, But Keep It Clean.

01:35:14.020 --> 01:35:16.240
Yeah, always a great idea, Sally.

01:35:16.440 --> 01:35:17.900
It's available at Supermarket. Check out somewhere.

01:35:18.060 --> 01:35:19.600
Yeah, I'll be looking for it, okay?

01:35:19.880 --> 01:35:21.160
Oh, $14.95!

01:35:21.520 --> 01:35:24.300
I'll be looking for you too, yeah, next week, right here in the Video Vault.

01:35:24.600 --> 01:35:26.960
I'm gonna be showing one of our favorites, boy.

01:35:27.800 --> 01:35:29.720
Ship of Zombies!

01:35:30.000 --> 01:35:33.940
Woo! That is 1 o'clock, Eastern and Pacific, 12 o'clock Central.

01:35:34.300 --> 01:35:36.830
Till then, keep your nose in the wind, your tail to yourself.

01:35:37.730 --> 01:35:38.370
See ya, Pilgrim.

